# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# Without this the context carries node_modules (hundreds of megabytes, and rebuilt inside the
# image anyway), plus anything local that matches a secret or a database — a `.env` sitting in the
# working directory would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon and, one careless `COPY .` later,
# baked into a published layer.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Built output. Every image builds from source; copying a host build in would ship whatever
# happened to be on that machine.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and local state.
.env
.env.*
!docker/.env.example
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*

.git
.github
spike

# Documentation and planning: not needed to build, and they change constantly, which would bust
# the context cache on every edit.
*.md
docs
